        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="0566" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg472"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McDonald to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Teheran, Persia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-04-27"><hi rendition="#italic">April 27, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received June 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 239, Dip. Ser.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am glad to be able to send a denial of
                    the alleged horrible massacre of Armenians and Jews at Van, reported in my No.
                    235 by ——— ———, of ———. From the same source I am now informed that the report
                    was a huge exaggeration, and has dwindled from 22,000 to <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >four!</hi> Perhaps this is a sample of the truth of other like rumors.</p>
                <p>Herewith I also beg to send a translation of a copy of a note from the Sadr Azem
                    on the same subject, omitted inadvertently from my No. 235.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alex. McDonald.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d374-a1.xml" xpointer="d374-a1"/>
